course: dictionary
lesson: 9615
title: Stronghold and places that hold firm
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A stronghold is a place that is strong and well defended, so it is hard for enemies to capture. Castles, forts and mountain hideouts were often strongholds. The word has two parts, strong and hold, so think of a place that holds firm.
explain: Read the context: «The Zaporizhian Sich below the Dnipro rapids was a Cossack stronghold where the council (rada) elected and could remove its leaders.» Look at the clues: Cossacks, a council, rapids. These show a fortified place where people stood their ground. Swap in "a strong, safe place" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The word has other meanings too. A stronghold can be a place where an idea, animal or plant is still strong: «The Highlands are a stronghold of the red squirrel.» In politics, it is an area where most people support one party. When you meet the word, read the sentence around it to find out which meaning fits.
fact: A stronghold is a strong, well-defended place, such as a castle or fort that is hard to attack.
fact: «Stronghold» can also mean a place where a group, idea, animal or plant is still strong and common.
fact: In politics, a stronghold is an area where most people support one party.
fact: «Last stronghold» means the final place that is still holding out.
fact: The word has two parts, strong and hold, which helps you remember that it is a place that holds firm.
exercise: «The Zaporizhian Sich was a Cossack stronghold on the Dnipro rapids.» What is a stronghold here? | *A strong, well-defended place | A town with no walls at all | A sweet shop by the river | A kind of small boat
exercise: «The Highlands are a stronghold of the red squirrel.» What does stronghold mean here? | A place where the red squirrel is still strong and common | A fast train that goes through the hills | A place where red squirrels are not allowed | *A place where red squirrels are still strong and common
exercise: In politics, a stronghold is an area where most people support one party. What is a political stronghold? | A large, empty hall for debates | *An area where most people back one party | An area where nobody ever votes | A list of party rules
test: Ella reads «The rebels fled to their mountain stronghold.» Where did the rebels go? | *A strong, well-defended hideout in the mountains | A quiet school library | A busy shopping street | A swimming pool by the sea
test: In a news report, «the party's stronghold» means | a stadium where football is played | the area where the party's office is closed | a list of the party's rules | *the area where most people vote for that party
exam: Jayden says a stronghold is always a castle. Is he right? | *No, a stronghold can be a castle or fort, a place where an idea or animal is still strong, or an area that votes for one party | Yes, a stronghold is always a castle | Yes, but only if it has a moat | Only in stories, never in real life
